Listen. Practice. Speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:20,010
Hello everyone and welcome to Business English Learning. This is your everyday English practice

3
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:21,890
for real work situations.

4
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:26,810
Hi everyone. We're really happy you're here today. My name is Mauro.

5
00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:33,130
And I'm Erica. In this podcast, we help you feel more confident using English at work,

6
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:36,210
especially in conversations that can feel stressful.

7
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:39,010
Yes, like talking to your boss.

8
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:42,970
Many learners tell us this is one of the hardest things to do in English.

9
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:44,090
That's true.

10
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:47,850
Even people with good English feel nervous in these situations.

11
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:53,330
So today's episode is all about business English at work, focusing on clear and polite

12
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:55,630
communication with your manager.

13
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:58,250
Don't worry if you don't understand everything.

14
00:00:58,250 --> 00:00:59,850
Just relax and listen.

15
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:01,730
Alright, let's begin.

16
00:01:01,730 --> 00:01:03,930
Hi Kevin, do you have a minute?

17
00:01:03,930 --> 00:01:04,930
Hi Emily.

18
00:01:04,930 --> 00:01:05,930
Yes I do.

19
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:08,930
Thank you. I really appreciate your time.

20
00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:10,930
Of course. What would you like to talk about?

21
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:15,930
I wanted to talk about my recent tasks and check if I'm on the right track.

22
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:17,930
That's a good thing to do. Go ahead.

23
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:22,930
I've been working on the customer follow-up project and the monthly report at the same time.

24
00:01:22,930 --> 00:01:25,930
Yes, I know it's been a busy period.

25
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:28,930
I just want to make sure I'm prioritizing correctly.

26
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:32,930
That makes sense. Which task feels the most challenging right now?

27
00:01:32,930 --> 00:01:36,610
The monthly report, especially the data analysis part.

28
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:41,730
I see. That section is important, but it doesn't need to be perfect on the first draft.

29
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:45,570
That's good to know. I was worried I was spending too much time on it.

30
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:49,170
It's okay. What matters is clarity, not perfection.

31
00:01:49,170 --> 00:01:53,570
Thanks. That helps a lot. Is there anything else you'd like feedback on?

32
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:57,730
Yes, actually. I wanted to ask about my communication in meetings.

33
00:01:57,730 --> 00:01:59,970
All right. How do you feel about it?

34
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:04,050
Sometimes I understand the discussion, but I hesitate to speak.

35
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:07,410
That's very common, especially in a second language.

36
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:09,890
I worry that my English isn't clear enough.

37
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:13,010
Your English is clear. You just need more confidence.

38
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:14,770
That's reassuring to hear.

39
00:02:14,770 --> 00:02:18,130
When you have an idea, try to share it, even if it's short.

40
00:02:18,130 --> 00:02:20,770
So it's okay if my sentence is simple.

41
00:02:20,770 --> 00:02:24,610
Absolutely. Simple English works very well in business.

42
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:26,690
That makes me feel more comfortable.

43
00:02:26,690 --> 00:02:30,690
Good. Clear communication is more important than complex language.

44
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:33,690
I also wanted to talk about deadlines this week.

45
00:02:33,690 --> 00:02:35,690
Sure. What's the situation?

46
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:40,690
The client call on Thursday and the report deadline on Friday feel a bit tight.

47
00:02:40,690 --> 00:02:43,690
I understand. Which one do you think needs more time?

48
00:02:43,690 --> 00:02:47,690
The client call preparation. I want to be fully ready.

49
00:02:47,690 --> 00:02:50,690
That's reasonable. Would one extra day for the report help?

50
00:02:50,690 --> 00:02:52,690
Yes, definitely.

51
00:02:52,690 --> 00:02:55,690
Okay. Let's move the report deadline to Monday.

52
00:02:55,690 --> 00:02:58,490
Thank you so much. I really appreciate that.

53
00:02:58,490 --> 00:03:01,690
No problem. I'd rather have good work than rushed work.

54
00:03:01,690 --> 00:03:03,290
I agree completely.

55
00:03:03,290 --> 00:03:06,330
You're doing well, Emily. Don't be too hard on yourself.

56
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:07,690
I'll try not to be.

57
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:10,490
Do you have any long-term goals you'd like to talk about?

58
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:14,890
Yes. I'd like to grow in the company and take on more responsibility.

59
00:03:14,890 --> 00:03:18,330
That's great to hear. I want to keep improving my skills.

60
00:03:18,330 --> 00:03:23,690
Focus on communication, planning, and confidence. You're already improving.

61
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:26,090
Thank you. That motivates me a lot.

62
00:03:26,090 --> 00:03:30,570
Anytime. My door is always open. I appreciate your support.

63
00:03:30,570 --> 00:03:32,650
You're a valuable part of the team.

64
00:03:32,650 --> 00:03:34,250
That means a lot to me.

65
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:36,490
All right. Let's catch up again next month.

66
00:03:36,490 --> 00:03:38,410
Sounds good. Thank you again.

67
00:03:38,410 --> 00:03:40,010
You're welcome. Have a great day.

68
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:40,890
You too.

69
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:43,610
And that's the end of today's conversation.

70
00:03:43,610 --> 00:03:48,330
Remember, you don't need perfect English to communicate well at work.

71
00:03:48,330 --> 00:03:50,650
Simple, clear English is enough.

72
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:52,890
Keep practicing. Keep improving.

73
00:03:52,890 --> 00:03:55,210
and we'll see you in the next episode.

74
00:03:56,330 --> 00:03:59,330
This is your everyday business English class.

75
