101
00:05:21,570 --> 00:05:26,050
Alright, grab your coffee, take a deep breath, and let's get started.

102
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:27,290
Good morning, Sarah.

103
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:29,130
Do you have a moment to talk?

104
00:05:29,130 --> 00:05:30,130
Good morning, Tom.

105
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:31,690
Yes, I have a few minutes.

106
00:05:31,690 --> 00:05:32,690
What's on your mind?

107
00:05:32,690 --> 00:05:33,690
Thank you.

108
00:05:33,690 --> 00:05:39,090
I wanted to give you a quick update on my current tasks and ask a few questions.

109
00:05:39,090 --> 00:05:40,090
That sounds good.

110
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:42,170
I appreciate you keeping me informed.

111
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:43,290
Please, go ahead.

112
00:05:43,290 --> 00:05:46,610
First, I wanted to talk about the marketing proposal.

113
00:05:46,610 --> 00:05:48,450
I finished the first draft.

114
00:05:48,450 --> 00:05:49,450
Great.

115
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:51,250
How do you feel about it so far?

116
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:56,970
I think the structure is clear, but I'm not sure if the tone is right for senior management.

117
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:58,850
That's a good question.

118
00:05:58,850 --> 00:06:01,810
The tone should be confident but simple.

119
00:06:01,810 --> 00:06:06,410
So less detail and more focus on key points?

120
00:06:06,410 --> 00:06:07,650
Exactly.

121
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:11,130
Senior managers usually want the mean message quickly.

122
00:06:11,130 --> 00:06:12,250
That helps a lot.

123
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:14,690
I'll revise it with that in mind.

124
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:15,690
Perfect.

125
00:06:15,690 --> 00:06:18,010
Do you think you can send the updated version?

126
00:06:18,010 --> 00:06:21,190
I can send it by tomorrow afternoon.

127
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,410
That works for me.

128
00:06:22,410 --> 00:06:24,570
Thank you for being clear about the timing.

129
00:06:24,570 --> 00:06:25,570
You're welcome.

130
00:06:25,570 --> 00:06:28,850
I also wanted to ask about priorities this week.

131
00:06:28,850 --> 00:06:29,850
Sure.

132
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:31,330
What are you concerned about?

133
00:06:31,330 --> 00:06:36,410
I'm working on the proposal, the client emails, and the internal report.

134
00:06:36,410 --> 00:06:39,490
I want to make sure I focus on the right things.

135
00:06:39,490 --> 00:06:40,850
I'm glad you asked.

136
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:43,130
The proposal is the top priority.

137
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:44,130
Okay.

138
00:06:44,130 --> 00:06:45,210
That's good to know.

139
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:50,490
The client emails are also important, but the internal report can wait until next week.

140
00:06:50,490 --> 00:06:51,490
That really helps.

141
00:06:51,490 --> 00:06:55,050
I was worried about trying to do everything at once.

142
00:06:55,050 --> 00:06:57,410
You don't need to do everything at the same time.

143
00:06:57,410 --> 00:07:00,010
It's better to do fewer things well.

144
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:01,090
I agree.

145
00:07:01,090 --> 00:07:03,090
Thank you for clarifying that.

146
00:07:03,090 --> 00:07:04,090
Of course.

147
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:06,290
Is there anything else you'd like to discuss?

148
00:07:06,290 --> 00:07:07,570
Yes, actually.

149
00:07:07,570 --> 00:07:10,930
I wanted to talk about a small challenge I'm having.

150
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,170
That's fine.

151
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:13,290
Please tell me.

152
00:07:13,290 --> 00:07:18,970
In meetings, sometimes I need more time to process information in English.

153
00:07:18,970 --> 00:07:20,850
That's completely understandable.

154
00:07:20,850 --> 00:07:23,610
What happens in those situations?

155
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:28,330
Sometimes the discussion moves very fast, and I hesitate to speak.

156
00:07:28,330 --> 00:07:29,770
Thank you for being honest.

157
00:07:29,770 --> 00:07:30,850
That's important.

158
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:33,890
I don't want people to think I don't have ideas.

159
00:07:33,890 --> 00:07:35,410
I understand.

160
00:07:35,410 --> 00:07:39,490
One thing you can do is prepare one or two points before meetings.

161
00:07:39,490 --> 00:07:40,890
That's a good idea.

162
00:07:40,890 --> 00:07:43,290
You can also say, can I add something?

163
00:07:43,290 --> 00:07:45,750
Or I'd like to comment on that.

164
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:48,770
Those phrases sound very useful and polite.

165
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:49,770
They are.

166
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:54,450
And remember, it's okay to ask people to slow down or repeat.

167
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:56,850
Sometimes I worry that will interrupt the meeting.

168
00:07:56,850 --> 00:07:59,330
Actually, it often helps everyone.

169
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:02,210
Clear communication benefits the whole team.

170
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:04,210
That makes me feel more confident.

171
00:08:04,210 --> 00:08:05,330
Good.

172
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:07,930
Confidence comes from practice, not perfection.

173
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:10,870
I'm trying to practice a little every day.

174
00:08:10,870 --> 00:08:12,390
That's the best approach.

175
00:08:12,390 --> 00:08:14,710
Even 10 minutes a day makes a difference.

176
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:18,670
I usually listen to English podcasts during my commute.

177
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:20,150
That's an excellent habit.

178
00:08:20,150 --> 00:08:21,150
Keep doing that.

179
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:22,150
Thank you.

180
00:08:22,150 --> 00:08:25,750
I also wanted to ask about my overall performance.

181
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:27,350
I'm glad you brought that up.

182
00:08:27,350 --> 00:08:29,070
How do you feel about your work?

183
00:08:29,070 --> 00:08:34,990
I feel motivated, but sometimes I'm not sure if I'm meeting expectations.

184
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:36,510
You are doing well, Tom.

185
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:39,230
Your work is reliable and consistent.

186
00:08:39,230 --> 00:08:40,830
That's great to hear.

187
00:08:40,830 --> 00:08:45,270
One area you can continue to develop is speaking up more in group discussions.

188
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:47,590
Yes, that makes sense.

189
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:50,910
But overall, I'm very happy with your progress.

190
00:08:50,910 --> 00:08:51,910
Thank you, Sarah.

191
00:08:51,910 --> 00:08:54,150
That feedback really encourages me.

192
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:55,230
You're welcome.

193
00:08:55,230 --> 00:08:58,230
Do you have any long-term goals you'd like to share?

194
00:08:58,230 --> 00:09:02,310
Yes, I'd like to take on more responsibility in the future.

195
00:09:02,310 --> 00:09:03,630
That's good to hear.

196
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:05,750
Growth starts with initiative.

197
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:08,030
What skills do you think I should focus on?

198
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:11,950
communication, time management, and decision making.

199
00:09:11,950 --> 00:09:13,510
I'll work on those.

200
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:16,790
And remember, you can always come to me with questions.

201
00:09:16,790 --> 00:09:18,150
I appreciate that.

202
00:09:18,150 --> 00:09:19,990
It makes a big difference.

203
00:09:19,990 --> 00:09:22,350
My door is always open.

204
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:24,350
Thank you for your time and support.

205
00:09:24,350 --> 00:09:25,750
You're very welcome.

206
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:27,230
Keep up the good work.

207
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:30,070
That was a very realistic workplace conversation.

208
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:35,710
Yes, and situations like this happen every day in offices around the world.

209
00:09:35,710 --> 00:09:40,670
Clear, polite, and simple English is enough to communicate well with your boss.

210
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:44,470
You don't need perfect grammar or advanced vocabulary.

211
00:09:44,470 --> 00:09:48,470
What matters most is being clear, respectful, and honest.

