00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,200
That's good to hear.

263
00:11:58,200 --> 00:12:00,500
I was hoping you could give me some feedback.

264
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:01,500
Of course.

265
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:05,040
Let's start with your last project, the client proposal.

266
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:07,740
Yes, that one. I worked hard on it.

267
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:11,940
You did. The structure was clear and your ideas were strong.

268
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:13,740
Thank you. That means a lot.

269
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:16,940
One thing you can improve is the introduction.

270
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:18,540
Could you explain what you mean?

271
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:21,640
Sure. It could be shorter and more direct.

272
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,540
So less detail at the beginning?

273
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:27,740
Exactly. Busy people want the main point fast.

274
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:30,040
Got it. I'll rewrite that part.

275
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,840
Great. Send me the new version when it's ready.

276
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,840
I will. Thanks for the suggestion.

277
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:37,480
You're welcome. Anything else on your mind?

278
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:40,680
Yes. I wanted to talk about my schedule this week.

279
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,280
Okay, what's going on?

280
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:44,760
I feel a bit overloaded with tasks.

281
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:47,480
Which task is the most challenging right now?

282
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,640
The team presentation on Wednesday.

283
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,560
Yes, that's an important one.

284
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:54,520
I want to do it well, but I'm worried about time.

285
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:57,080
I appreciate that you care about quality.

286
00:12:57,080 --> 00:13:00,040
Would it be possible to move one of my other deadlines?

287
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,080
Which one?

288
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:04,040
The internal report. Maybe until Friday?

289
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:06,040
That's reasonable. Let's do that.

290
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:08,360
Thank you so much. That helps a lot.

291
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:11,560
Good communication makes work easier for everyone.

292
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,800
I'm trying to communicate better in English.

293
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:17,160
You're doing very well. Your English has improved a lot.

294
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:19,800
Really? I still feel nervous sometimes.

295
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:23,000
That's normal. Confidence comes with practice.

296
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,640
I try to listen to English podcasts every day.

297
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:27,960
That's a great habit. Keep doing that.

298
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,760
In meetings, I don't always understand everything.

299
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:32,360
That happens to everyone.

300
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:34,440
Is it okay to ask people to repeat?

301
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:37,160
Of course! It's professional, not rude.

302
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,280
What can I say?

303
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,400
You can say,

304
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,320
sorry, could you say that again?

305
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:44,440
Or just to make sure I understand.

306
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:45,720
That sounds helpful.

307
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:48,280
Always ask questions, that's how you learn.

308
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:50,360
Thanks. One more thing.

309
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:52,120
I'd like to grow in the company.

310
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,400
That's great to hear.

311
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:54,840
What should I focus on?

312
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:58,600
Communication, time management, and confidence.

313
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,800
I'll work on those.

314
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,260
and don't be afraid to share your ideas.

315
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:03,660
I'll try to speak up more.

316
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:05,740
Good. Your ideas matter.

317
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:08,580
Thank you, Emma. I really appreciate your support.

318
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:11,380
Anytime, Alex. My door is always open.

319
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:12,380
Have a great day.

320
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:14,180
You too. Keep up the good work.

321
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:17,220
That was a very natural workplace conversation.

322
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:21,980
Yes, and these kinds of talks happen every day in offices around the world.

323
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:23,980
Let's quickly review what you learned today.

324
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:27,140
You learned how to ask for feedback politely.

325
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:29,940
How to talk about deadlines without sounding negative.

326
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:33,140
How to ask for clarification when you don't understand.

327
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:36,020
And how to talk about growth and goals at work.

328
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:39,220
Remember, you don't need perfect English.

329
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:42,180
You need clear, simple and confident English.

330
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:44,580
So here's your challenge for this week.

331
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:47,620
Use one sentence from today's episode in real life.

332
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:49,940
Or practice it out loud at home.

333
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:52,500
Small steps create big progress.

334
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:55,380
If this episode helped you, subscribe.

